description:
Build a growing array of ints in `solution.c`. The struct is given; write the functions:

```c
struct int_list {
    int *items;
    size_t length;
    size_t capacity;
};

void list_init(struct int_list *list);            /* empty: items NULL, length and capacity 0 */
bool list_push(struct int_list *list, int value); /* adds at the end; false if memory ran out */
bool list_pop(struct int_list *list, int *out);   /* removes the last into *out; false when empty */
long long list_sum(const struct int_list *list);
void list_free(struct int_list *list);            /* frees the items and makes the list empty again */
```

When a push finds the list full, the capacity grows from 0 to **4**, and after that **doubles** (4, 8, 16, ...). The tests check the capacity. Use `realloc`, assigning its result to a temporary first.

